# V1 feature architecture (normative)

**Before implementing or refactoring anything under `apps/webapp`, read:**

[`docs/specs/v1-feature-architecture-spec.md`](../../docs/specs/v1-feature-architecture-spec.md)

That spec is **what to build**. Pair it with:

- [`docs/specs/app-shell-spec.md`](../../docs/specs/app-shell-spec.md) — list · drawer · modals
- [`docs/specs/data-loading-spec.md`](../../docs/specs/data-loading-spec.md) — PageQuery · entity store · mutations
- [`docs/specs/design-language-spec.md`](../../docs/specs/design-language-spec.md) — visuals

Progress / gaps only: [`docs/reference/ui-architecture-reference.md`](../../docs/reference/ui-architecture-reference.md) (not normative).

## Must follow

1. **Classify the entity** — complex (URL drawer) · simple (row `···` only) · thin drawer · layout variant.
2. **Toolbar** — `[Primary CTA] [Search] [Main filter <select>] [Filter] [More]`; no chip-bar main filters.
3. **Locked routes** — assessments at `/evaluations` (all `kind`s); no `/homework` nav; no `/configuration/roles`; no resource UI in v1.
4. **Staff permissions** — Staff drawer → Permissions tab (`staffPermissionAssignments`), not a roles matrix screen.
5. **Class attendance** — `attendanceMode` on class config; `/attendance` nav only when `daily`; daily = list of days + drawer.
6. **Incidents** — resolve via **`resolveIncidentWithOutcomes`** in one modal; involved students read-only in drawer.
7. **Assessments** — one drawer; exclusive body section by `kind`; homework is `kind = homework` on evaluations.
8. **Do not** invent parallel routes or drawers for simple entities (Fee, Payment, GradeScale, DisciplinaryAction).

## Agent checklist (every screen)

- [ ] Route matches §6 route index in the v1 spec
- [ ] Surface type matches entity (§3)
- [ ] Locked UX decisions respected (§4)
- [ ] app-shell + data-loading specs followed
- [ ] Update progress in `ui-architecture-reference.md` when the feature reaches target
